## Conclusion

The core Fulu proposer lookahead mechanism is implemented correctly with appropriate bounds checking. The trust boundary between the lookahead-based and on-demand computation paths is well-guarded for the current and next epoch (the primary use case). The most notable finding (SA-003) is that Fulu-era states asked for far-future epochs (stateEpoch+2 or beyond) silently fall through to legacy on-demand computation rather than returning an error, which could produce results based on unfinished RANDAO randomness -- though no known caller exercises this path.

